.TH SDL_IOFromConstMem 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_IOFromConstMem \- Use this function to prepare a read-only memory buffer for use with
.BR SDL_IOStream .

.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_iostream.h>
.PP
.BI "SDL_IOStream * SDL_IOFromConstMem(const void *mem, size_t size);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
This function sets up an
.BR SDL_IOStream
struct based on a memory area of a certain size\[char46] It assumes the memory area is not writable\[char46]
.PP
Attempting to write to this
.BR SDL_IOStream
stream will report an error without writing to the memory buffer\[char46]
.PP
This memory buffer is not copied by the
.BR SDL_IOStream ;
the pointer you provide must remain valid until you close the stream\[char46]
.PP
If you need to write to a memory buffer, you should use
.BR SDL_IOFromMem ()
with a writable buffer of memory instead\[char46]
.PP
The following properties will be set at creation time by SDL:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_MEMORY_POINTER :
this will be the
.BR mem
parameter that was passed to this function\[char46]
.PP
\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_MEMORY_SIZE_NUMBER :
this will be the
.BR size
parameter that was passed to this function\[char46]
.PP
Additionally, the following properties are recognized:
.PP

\(bu
.BR SDL_PROP_IOSTREAM_MEMORY_FREE_FUNC_POINTER :
if this property is set to a non-NULL value it will be interpreted as a function of
.BR SDL_free_func
type and called with the passed
.BR mem
pointer when closing the stream\[char46] By default it is unset, i\[char46]e\[char46], the memory will not be freed\[char46]

.SH FUNCTION PARAMETERS
.TP
.I mem
a pointer to a read-only buffer to feed an
.BR SDL_IOStream
stream\[char46]
.TP
.I size
the buffer size, in bytes\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns a pointer to a new
.BR SDL_IOStream
structure or NULL on failure; call
.BR SDL_GetError ()
for more information\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this function from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This function is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

